@startuml
title ThingsBoard 3.6 Telemetry Query: keys, latest, raw range and aggregation
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Microsoft YaHei"
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #1F2937
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #374151
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participantBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam participantFontColor #111827
skinparam actorBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam actorBackgroundColor #EAF7FB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF7D6
skinparam noteBorderColor #92400E
skinparam noteFontColor #111827
skinparam groupBorderColor #374151
skinparam groupHeaderBackgroundColor #E5E7EB
skinparam groupFontColor #111827
skinparam databaseBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #ECFDF5
skinparam collectionsBorderColor #1F2937
skinparam collectionsBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.6
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
hide footbox

actor "REST Client" as Client
participant "Spring MVC" as MVC
participant "TelemetryController" as Controller
participant "AccessValidator" as Access
participant "BaseTimeseriesService" as Service
participant "TimeseriesLatestDao" as LatestDao
participant "TimeseriesDao" as HistoryDao
database "PostgreSQL\nSQL DAO" as PostgreSQL
database "TimescaleDB\nTimescale DAO" as Timescale
database "Cassandra\nCassandra DAO" as Cassandra
participant "TbGetTelemetryNode" as RuleNode

== Common REST and permission boundary ==
Client -> MVC : GET /api/plugins/telemetry/{type}/{id}/...
MVC -> Controller : mapped GET method
Controller -> Access : validateEntityAndCallback(user, READ_TELEMETRY, entityId, callback)
Access --> Controller : return new DeferredResult immediately
Access -> Access : validate entity and accessControlService permission
alt entity missing or access denied
  Access -> MVC : response.setResult(error)
  MVC --> Client : HTTP error
else allowed
  Access -> Controller : invoke callback(response, tenantId, entityId)
end
note over MVC,Access
  DeferredResult has no local timeout.
  spring.mvc.async.request-timeout defaults to 30000 ms.
end note

== Keys query ==
Controller -> Service : findAllLatest(tenantId, entityId)
Service -> LatestDao : findAllLatest(tenantId, entityId)
alt database.ts_latest.type is sql or timescale
  LatestDao -> PostgreSQL : SELECT latest rows JOIN ts_kv_dictionary
  PostgreSQL --> LatestDao : existing latest rows
else database.ts_latest.type is cassandra
  LatestDao -> Cassandra : SELECT all keys and values from ts_kv_latest_cf partition
  Cassandra --> LatestDao : existing latest rows
end
LatestDao --> Service : Future<List<TsKvEntry>>
Service --> Controller : callback with latest entries
Controller -> Controller : extract unique entry keys
Controller -> MVC : DeferredResult.setResult(key array)
MVC --> Client : HTTP 200 JSON array
note over Controller,LatestDao
  The keys endpoint reads latest storage.
  It does not scan history for DISTINCT keys.
end note

== Latest values query ==
Client -> MVC : GET values/timeseries?keys=k1,k2
MVC -> Controller : getLatestTimeseries(type, id, keys, strictTypes)
Controller -> Access : validate READ_TELEMETRY
Access -> Controller : invoke allowed callback
alt keys parameter is empty
  Controller -> Service : findAllLatest(tenantId, entityId)
  Service -> LatestDao : one findAllLatest query
else keys were requested
  loop one Future per key
    Controller -> Service : findLatest(tenantId, entityId, key)
    Service -> LatestDao : findLatest(tenantId, entityId, key)
    alt SQL latest
      LatestDao -> PostgreSQL : getOrSaveKeyId(key), SELECT by entityId and keyId
    else Cassandra latest
      LatestDao -> Cassandra : SELECT by entityType, entityId and text key
    end
  end
  Service -> Service : Futures.allAsList(per-key futures)
end
alt requested key exists
  LatestDao --> Service : stored timestamp and typed value
else requested key is absent
  LatestDao --> Service : current server timestamp and null StringDataEntry
end
Service --> Controller : List<TsKvEntry>
Controller -> Controller : group by key; string or strict typed values
Controller -> MVC : DeferredResult.setResult(ResponseEntity 200)
MVC --> Client : key -> [{ts,value}]

== Raw history range ==
Client -> MVC : GET values/timeseries?keys=...&startTs=...&endTs=...&agg=NONE
MVC -> Controller : getTimeseries(...)
Controller -> Controller : one BaseReadTsKvQuery per key
Controller -> Service : findAll(tenantId, entityId, queries)
Service -> Service : validate each query
opt entityId is ENTITY_VIEW
  Service -> Service : load view, filter keys, clamp range, map origin entity
end
Service -> HistoryDao : findAllAsync(tenantId, entityId, queries)
par PostgreSQL history
  HistoryDao -> PostgreSQL : SELECT ts_kv WHERE entity/key and start <= ts < end ORDER BY ts LIMIT
  PostgreSQL --> HistoryDao : per-key rows
else Timescale history
  HistoryDao -> Timescale : same logical range query; chunk pruning
  Timescale --> HistoryDao : per-key rows
else Cassandra history
  HistoryDao -> Cassandra : discover ts_kv_partitions_cf partitions
  loop partitions in query order until per-key limit is full
    HistoryDao -> Cassandra : SELECT ts_kv_cf partition ORDER BY ts LIMIT remaining
    Cassandra --> HistoryDao : partition rows
  end
end
HistoryDao --> Service : List<ReadTsKvQueryResult>
Service -> Service : flatten results into List<TsKvEntry>
Service --> Controller : Future success
Controller -> Controller : LinkedHashMap grouping by key
Controller -> MVC : set HTTP response
MVC --> Client : raw points per key
note over Controller,HistoryDao
  Range is half-open [startTs, endTs).
  limit applies independently to every key.
  No offset or cursor is exposed by this REST endpoint.
end note

== Aggregation history ==
Client -> MVC : range query with AVG, SUM, MIN, MAX or COUNT
MVC -> Controller : getTimeseries(... agg, interval or calendar ...)
Controller -> Controller : AggregationParams and one query per key
Controller -> Service : findAll(...)
Service -> Service : validate interval count using max(interval, 1000)
alt database.ts.type is sql
  loop each key and each bucket
    Service -> HistoryDao : findAllAsync(query bucket)
    HistoryDao -> PostgreSQL : one aggregate SQL for [bucketStart,bucketEnd)
    PostgreSQL --> HistoryDao : optional aggregate row
  end
else database.ts.type is timescale and interval is milliseconds
  loop each key
    HistoryDao -> Timescale : one time_bucket query for full range
    Timescale --> HistoryDao : ordered bucket rows
    opt partial final bucket
      HistoryDao -> Timescale : separate tail aggregate query
      Timescale --> HistoryDao : tail row
    end
  end
else database.ts.type is timescale and interval is calendar
  loop each key and calendar period
    HistoryDao -> Timescale : one aggregate query for calculated period
    Timescale --> HistoryDao : optional period row
  end
else database.ts.type is cassandra
  loop each key and logical bucket
    HistoryDao -> Cassandra : discover all partitions crossing bucket
    par concurrent partial aggregate reads
      HistoryDao -> Cassandra : aggregate CQL for partition 1
    else
      HistoryDao -> Cassandra : aggregate CQL for partition N
    end
    Cassandra --> HistoryDao : partial results
    HistoryDao -> HistoryDao : AggregatePartitionsFunction.merge
  end
end
HistoryDao --> Service : non-empty bucket entries at bucket midpoint
Service --> Controller : flat entries
Controller -> MVC : JSON response
MVC --> Client : aggregate curve
note over Service,Timescale
  ThingsBoard 3.6 does runtime time_bucket aggregation.
  No Continuous Aggregate is created by the install/query code.
end note

== Rule Engine internal caller ==
RuleNode -> RuleNode : onMsg(ctx, msg), build FIRST/LAST/ALL queries
RuleNode -> Service : findAll(tenantId, msg.originator, queries)
Service -> HistoryDao : selected history backend
HistoryDao --> Service : asynchronous query results
alt Future succeeds
  Service --> RuleNode : List<TsKvEntry>
  RuleNode -> RuleNode : write values into TbMsg metadata
  RuleNode -> RuleNode : ctx.tellSuccess(msg)
else Future fails
  Service --> RuleNode : throwable
  RuleNode -> RuleNode : ctx.tellFailure(msg, throwable)
end
note over RuleNode,HistoryDao
  The node is already running inside Rule Engine context.
  It does not publish another Kafka message for the database read.
end note

== Failure and timeout boundary ==
alt DAO Future fails normally
  HistoryDao --> Controller : onFailure(throwable)
  Controller -> Controller : log error and AccessValidator.handleError
  Controller -> MVC : HTTP 500 result
else Cassandra raw callback only logs and leaves Future incomplete
  Cassandra --> HistoryDao : driver failure
  HistoryDao -> HistoryDao : log without setException in selected paths
  ... Spring MVC async timeout ...
  MVC --> Client : asynchronous request timeout
else client disconnects first
  Client -> MVC : connection closed
  note over MVC,HistoryDao
    Source has no explicit cancellation propagation
    from DeferredResult/client disconnect to the database Future.
  end note
end

@enduml
